-- erwartet: N030
-- **669 -- the two axes of a DMA buffer, mixed AT A FIELD.**
--
-- `N030` has held nominal types since 2026-08-20, and `beispiele/gift/200` says why it had
-- to grow past the call: *"the class right and then one instance repaired."* It grew to the
-- binding, the return and the comparison, and it stopped at a BARE name.
--
-- **A field is where two axes actually live**, and that is not a guess about hypothetical
-- programs. Caprock keeps the CPU view and the device view of one DMA buffer in ONE record
-- (`caprock-virtio/src/owned.rs`:70-77) and names the bug in its own note: with an IOMMU
-- window != 0 the two numbers differ, and a driver that mixes them programmes the device an
-- address it cannot resolve. Caprock buys the guarantee with FIELD PRIVACY. Gabbro has none
-- and does not need it -- `opaque` makes the mixing a TYPE error rather than a convention
-- about which getter to call.
--
-- > **The bundling cannot simply be dropped.** Passing the two views as separate parameters
-- > is where `N030` already bit, and it gives up the thing the record exists for: that these
-- > two numbers are the two views of the SAME buffer.
--
-- Two sites, and the second one is the interesting half: a `let` that takes the field first
-- makes the mistake one line longer, and until 2026-09-03 that was enough to lose it.

module gift {

opaque type Cpusicht     = u64;
opaque type Geraetesicht = u64;

type Zweiachser = {
    cpu    : Cpusicht,
    dev    : Geraetesicht,
    laenge : u32,
};

extern fn deskriptor_stellen(adresse : Geraetesicht, laenge : u32)
    effects { pure }
    costs   <= 8 ops;

impl fn am_feld(p : ptr<normal, r> Zweiachser)
    effects { reads p }
    costs   <= 16 ops
{
    deskriptor_stellen(p.cpu, p.laenge);
}

impl fn ueber_eine_bindung(p : ptr<normal, r> Zweiachser)
    effects { reads p }
    costs   <= 16 ops
{
    let c = p.cpu;
    deskriptor_stellen(c, p.laenge);
}

}
